  "expectedDraftMasterHash": "sha256:e4b50e29845ca15550a9998270846632bd0f12e48fe7d12873359427d4507d5c",
  "visualBrief": "Madrid headquarters exterior with a red-brick main block, pale stone courses, eleven-bay north front and balcony, a four-column Doric portico and granite stairs on the west side, and the projecting brick rear wing and tall windows on Calle Moreto. The low slate roof retains eight chimneys. Garden fences and surrounding streets remain part of the map context.",
  "heightPolicy": "The modeled main block measures about 28.4 by 44.2 m, with a 20 m cornice, 21.4 m roof and 23.4 m chimney caps. PMTiles records a coarse 8 m height. The model uses photo-based proportions. The original viewer terrain determines the west stair toe and rises toward the rear wing. The stair run has been fitted to the standard field and surveyed thresholds remain unknown.",
  "nativeAxes": "+X north along Calle de Felipe IV, +Z east toward the rear wing on Calle Moreto, -Z west toward the portico and Ruiz de Alarcón, +Y up.",
