  "limitations": [
    "The modeled main block measures about 28.4 by 44.2 m, with a 20 m cornice, 21.4 m roof and 23.4 m chimney caps. PMTiles records a coarse 8 m height. The model uses photo-based proportions. The original viewer terrain determines the west stair toe and rises toward the rear wing. The stair run has been fitted to the standard field and surveyed thresholds remain unknown.",
    "The garden photo confirms the west portico and its broad granite stairs. The rear street photo shows a solid brick projection with tall upper windows, stone spandrels and a shallow cap. Stair count, rear decorative details, garden furniture and exact terrain grades are approximations.",
    "Seven shared 256 px brick, limestone, granite, slate, wood, painted metal and punched-window graphs. Materials use metric UVs and linear colors. Skyline combines the main shell, both projections and the roof in one material group. The closer levels add recesses, masonry ornament and fluted columns."
  ],
  "references": [
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sede_de_la_Real_Academia_Espa%C3%B1ola.jpg",
      "observed": "Northwest corner shows the brick west front, garden fence, four-column Doric portico, high pale attic band and the adjacent eleven-bay north elevation."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sede_de_la_R.A.E._(Madrid)_02.jpg",
      "observed": "Actually inspected the full north frontage: eleven bays on both brick stories, central closed secondary door with small stone balcony above, alternating triangular and horizontal upper window heads, continuous pale belt/base courses, tall narrow attic windows alternating square relief panels, dentil cornice and several brick chimneys. Ground and basement follow a slight street slope. Exact sculptural/lettered detail is omitted in favor of original geometric interpretation."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_back_of_the_RAE.jpg",
      "observed": "Rear projection has a broad brick face, tall shallow-arched windows, stone spandrels, corner pilasters and a low cornice. Visible uphill sidewalk and south-side basement windows."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.rae.es/la-institucion/la-rae/sede-institucional/descubra-la-rae/exteriores",
      "observed": "Four fluted columns, three recessed doors and a broad flight of granite steps face the garden. The garden entrance faces Ruiz de Alarcón."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://build.protomaps.com/20261031.pmtiles",
      "observed": "The source location resolves the institution Q11993457 to its Madrid headquarters Q26960988. Standard PMTiles places the named POI and its building under feature 35184457607397. The west-facing columned portico overlooks Ruiz de Alarcón. The solid rear wing on Calle Moreto occupies the eastward map projection. The north front preserves its balcony and secondary door."
    }
  ],
